        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Cartagena, Chess\n- People: Leo Colovini, Adolf Albin\n- Topics: Board games, Chess, Pirate jailbreak theme\n\nFacts:\n- Cartagena is a German-style board game that was released in 2000.\n- Cartagena takes its theme from the legendary 1672 pirate-led jailbreak from the fortress of Cartagena.\n- Chess is a two-player strategy board game played on a checkered 8×8 chessboard with 64 squares.\n- Chess is played by millions of people worldwide.\n- Adolf Albin was a Romanian chess player who lived from 14 September 1848 to 1 February 1920.\n- Leo Colovini's most popular game is Cartagena.",
